  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Green Chemicals in Water Treatment (GREENCHEM) in Asia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The GREENCHEM project aims to address challenges in algae-impaired water (AIW) treatment by introducing an innovative green chemical developed by FerrTech, named Fersol&#xa9;. This sustainable alternative to traditional pre-chlorination enhanced coagulation offers improved water quality, lower treatment costs, reduced environmental impact, and simpler engineering. The project, conducted in Taiwan, will assess the feasibility of Fersol&#xa9; for algae and algal toxin mitigation in local AIW for drinking purposes. During this feasibility study, the consortium will identify local treatment challenges, estimate improvements, evaluate the project&#x2019;s strengths and weaknesses, and develop a pilot-scale implementation roadmap.</narrative>
  </description>
